The ReSTIR story's one-dimensional example of bias
==================================================

What the story draws on the canvas (lab/src/math/) for chapter 6's beats `c6-1d` and `c6-fix`: the paper's Fig. 7
redrawn from the lab's runs of it (demos/bias.rs): the target ramp, the flat and the step distributions, the true
inverse of RIS's output density (the thick line), and the mean of W (the thin line), as `biasReveal` draws them,
for the candidates, weight, and step of `biasCandidates`, `biasWeight`, and `biasNearZero`, with a marker at
`biasMark`. Beside the plot, one stage per sentence of the two beats as `biasStage` goes from 0 to 31: what the
lines are, the count W divides by, Eq. 19, the fix, the near-zero step's huge weights, the balance heuristic, and
Talbot's weight, whose cost the grid of every candidate and every distribution shows.

$[Import* std]
$[Import* render_lab_runtime]
$[Import* render_lab_math]
$[Import* paper_restir_values]
$[Import* paper_restir_natives]
$[Import* paper_restir_common]

The layout

The plot's box, the right column's centre, and the size of its formulas.
$[# _plotBox [% {box {v2 -6.6 -2.6} {v2 0.6 2.8}}]]
$[# _rightX 4.1]
$[# _size 0.44]
The rows of the right column: the legend's, then three for what each sentence adds.
$[# _slotB 0.5]
$[# _slotC -0.8]
$[# _slotD -2.1]
The step's colour, beside the flat distribution's (`pColor`), and the two lines'.
$[# _stepColor "#b48cff"]
$[# _truthColor "#6be3b0"]
$[# _meanColor "#ffa14a"]

Fn([Float, Float, Float, List(Mob)], List(Mob)). A figure shown from stage `a` (faded in) to stage `b` (faded out).
$[# {_during s a b fig} {!if {!or {< s a} {> s b}}
    {'}
    {fadeOut {phase s {- b 0.25} b} {fadeIn {phase s a {+ a 0.3}} fig}}}]

Fn([String, String, String, Float, Bool], List(Mob)). A legend row at height y: a swatch of the curve's colour,
thick or thin, and its formula beside it.
$[# {_legend id latex color y thick}
    [# swatch {line {++ id "Swatch"} {v2 1.7 y} {v2 2.3 y} color {!if thick 6.0 2.5}}]
    {append swatch {nextTo {tex id latex 0.4 color} swatch right 0.2}}]

The plot

Fn([Axes, List(Float), Float, String, Float], List(Mob)). A curve of per-bin values drawn as far as `upTo` across,
each value at its bin's middle (clamped to the plot's top).
$[# {_binned id ax values upTo color width}
    [# n {length values}]
    [# points {filter
        {map {range 0 n} {^ {i} {v2 {/ {+ {float i} 0.5} {float n}} {min 4.0 {nth values i}}}}}
        {^ {p} {<= {.x p} upTo}}}]
    {!if {< {length points} 2}
        {'}
        {pathThrough id {map points {^ {p} {onAxes ax {.x p} {.y p}}}} color width}}]

Fn([Axes, Float, Float, Float, {meanW: List(Float), runs: Int, truth: List(Float)}], List(Mob)). The plot: the
axes, then each curve as far as `reveal` has drawn it (the target, the flat PDF, the step, the thick line, the thin
line), and the marker at `mark` (none below 0).
$[# {_plot ax reveal mark near c}
    [# {_upTo n} {clamp {- reveal n} 0.0 1.0}]
    [# {_curve id f n color width} {!if {< {_upTo n} 0.01}
        {'}
        {plot id ax f 0.0 {_upTo n} color width}}]
    [# bins {length {.truth c}}]
    [# bin {clamp {floor {* mark {float bins}}} 0 {- bins 1}}]
    [# marker {!if {< mark 0.0}
        {'}
        {flatten {'
            {line "marker" {onAxes ax mark 0.0} {onAxes ax mark 4.0} accentColor 2.5}
            {!if {< reveal 4.0}
                {'}
                {dotAt "markTruth" {onAxes ax mark {min 4.0 {nth {.truth c} bin}}} 0.1 _truthColor}}
            {!if {< reveal 5.0}
                {'}
                {dotAt "markMean"
                    {onAxes ax mark {min 4.0 {nth {.meanW c} bin}}}
                    0.08
                    _meanColor}}}}}]
    {flatten {'
        {axesFigure "axes" ax textDimColor 0.34 true true}
        {_curve "target" biasTarget 0.0 targetColor 3.0}
        {_curve "flat" {^ {x} {biasPdf 0 x near}} 1.0 pColor 2.5}
        {_curve "step" {^ {x} {biasPdf 1 x near}} 2.0 _stepColor 2.5}
        {_binned "truth" ax {.truth c} {_upTo 3.0} _truthColor 7.0}
        {_binned "mean" ax {.meanW c} {_upTo 4.0} _meanColor 2.5}
        marker}}]

Fn([Float], List(Mob)). The legend, each row as its curve is drawn.
$[# {_legends reveal} {flatten {'
    {!if {< reveal 0.05} {'} {_legend "lTarget" f"{\hat p(x) = 2 - 2x}" targetColor 3.15 false}}
    {!if {< reveal 1.05} {'} {_legend "lFlat" f"{p_1}" pColor 2.65 false}}
    {!if {< reveal 2.05} {'} {_legend "lStep" f"{p_2}" _stepColor 2.15 false}}
    {!if {< reveal 3.05} {'} {_legend "lTruth" f"{1 / p_{\mathrm{RIS}}(x)}" _truthColor 1.65 true}}
    {!if {< reveal 4.05} {'} {_legend "lMean" f"{\overline{W}(x)}" _meanColor 1.15 false}}}}]

What each sentence adds

Fn([Float, Axes, Int, Float, Float], List(Mob)). The candidates in a row at slot C: the flat ones and the step
ones, the step ones struck out where the marker is past the step (they cannot produce y), and the count that could.
$[# {_candidates s m mark near}
    [# could {+ {div m 2} {!if {> {biasPdf 1 {max mark 0.0} near} 0.0} {div m 2} 0}}]
    [# xs {map {range 0 m} {^ {i} {+ {- _rightX {* 0.13 {float {- m 1}}}} {* 0.26 {float i}}}}}]
    [# dots {flatten {map
        {range 0 m}
        {^ {i} {dotAt f"{cand${str i}}"
            {v2 {nth xs i} {+ _slotC 0.35}}
            0.09
            {!if {= {% i 2} 0} pColor _stepColor}}}}}]
    [# steps {map {filter {range 0 m} {^ {i} {= {% i 2} 1}}} {^ {i} f"{cand${str i}}"}}]
    [# struck {!if {< could m} {crossParts {phase s 0.0 1.0} dots steps accentColor} dots}]
    {append struck {moveTo
        {tex "could" f"{|Z(y)| = ${str could} \quad M = ${str m}}" _size textColor}
        {v2 _rightX {- _slotC 0.35}}}}]

Fn([Float, Int, Float, {meanW: List(Float), runs: Int, truth: List(Float)}], List(Mob)). At the marker: the two
lines' values there and their ratio.
$[# {_atMarker mark c}
    [# bins {length {.truth c}}]
    [# bin {clamp {floor {* {max mark 0.0} {float bins}}} 0 {- bins 1}}]
    [# truth {nth {.truth c} bin}]
    [# mean {nth {.meanW c} bin}]
    {moveTo
        {texParts "atMark" f"{\lit{1}{\overline{W}} \cdot \lit{2}{p} = \frac{${numberLatex mean 2}}{${numberLatex truth 2}} = ${numberLatex {over mean truth} 2}}" _size textColor
            {' "W" "p"}
            {' _meanColor _truthColor}}
        {v2 _rightX _slotD}}]

Fn([Float, Int, Float], List(Mob)). Talbot's cost at slot C and D: a grid of every candidate (rows) and every
distribution (columns), all lit, then only the kept sample's row lit (the paper's weight), with their counts.
$[# {_grid s m}
    [# n {max m 2}]
    [# cell {/ 2.4 {float n}}]
    [# x0 {- _rightX 1.2}]
    [# y0 {- _slotC 0.2}]
    [# one {smooth {phase s 30.0 30.6}}]
    [# cells {flatten {map
        {range 0 {* n n}}
        {^ {k}
            [# r {div k n}]
            [# col {% k n}]
            [# lit {!if {= r 0} 1.0 {- 1.0 {* 0.85 one}}}]
            {filled f"{cell${str k}}"
                {box
                    {v2 {+ x0 {* cell {float col}}} {- y0 {* cell {float {+ r 1}}}}}
                    {v2 {+ x0 {* cell {+ {float col} 0.85}}} {- y0 {* cell {+ {float r} 0.15}}}}}
                {!if {= r 0} accentColor targetColor}
                {* 0.8 lit}}}}}]
    [# count {!if {< s 30.0} f"{n^2 = ${str {* n n}}}" f"{n = ${str n}}"}]
    {append cells {moveTo {tex "gridCount" count _size textColor} {v2 {- _rightX 2.0} {- y0 1.2}}}}]

Fn([Float, Float, Int, Float, Axes, {meanW: List(Float), runs: Int, truth: List(Float)}], List(Mob)). What the
sentence at stage s adds beside the plot (and on it).
$[# {_beside s mark m near ax c}
    [# {_at y fig} {moveTo fig {v2 _rightX y}}]
    [# {_rule id latex names colors} {_at _slotB {texParts id latex _size textColor names colors}}]
    [# halves {flatten {'
        {_during s 8.0 9.0 {filled "leftHalf"
            {box {onAxes ax 0.0 0.0} {onAxes ax 0.5 4.0}}
            _truthColor
            0.22}}
        {_during s 9.0 10.0 {filled "rightHalf"
            {box {onAxes ax 0.5 0.0} {onAxes ax 1.0 4.0}}
            pColor
            0.22}}}}]
    [# runs {append
        {_at _slotB {tex "runsF" f"{1 / p_{\mathrm{RIS}}(x)}" _size _truthColor}}
        {_at _slotC {tex "runsN" f"{${str {.runs c}}}" _size textColor}}}]
    [# huge {_at _slotD {tex "huge" f"{w = \frac{\hat p(y)}{p_2(y)} = \frac{${numberLatex {biasTarget {max mark 0.0}} 2}}{${numberLatex {biasPdf 1 {max mark 0.0} near} 4}} = ${short {over {biasTarget {max mark 0.0}} {biasPdf 1 {max mark 0.0} near}}}}" _size
        textColor}}]
    [# dark {moveTo
        {caption "darkNote" {textKey "sourcemath-dark"} 0.32 _meanColor}
        {onAxes ax 0.75 2.6}}]
    [# neighbour {moveTo
        {caption "neighbourNote" {textKey "biasmath-neighbour"} 0.32 _stepColor}
        {onAxes ax 0.3 2.35}}]
    {flatten {'
        halves
        {_during s 5.0 7.0 {append runs {_at
            {- _slotC 0.55}
            {caption "runsNote" {textKey "biasmath-runs"} 0.3 textDimColor}}}}
        {_during s 7.0 9.0 {_rule "should" f"{\lit{1}{\overline{W}(x)} = \lit{2}{1 / p_{\mathrm{RIS}}(x)}}"
            {' "W" "p"}
            {' _meanColor _truthColor}}}
        {_during s 10.0 12.0 {pointParts
            {phase s 10.3 11.0}
            {_rule "divides" f"{W = \frac{\sum w_i}{\lit{1}{M}\,\hat p(y)}}"
                {' "M"}
                {' accentColor}}
            {' "M"}
            accentColor}}
        {_during s 10.0 13.0 {_candidates {phase s 10.4 11.0} m mark near}}
        {_during s 11.0 15.0 {_atMarker mark c}}
        {_during s 12.0 17.0 {_rule "eq19" f"{E[W \mid y] = \frac{1}{p(y)} \cdot \frac{\lit{1}{|Z(y)|}}{\lit{2}{M}}}"
            {' "Z" "M"}
            {' accentColor accentColor}}}
        {_during s 14.0 15.0 dark}
        {_during s 15.0 17.0 neighbour}
        {_during s 17.0 23.0 {_rule "fix" f"{W = \frac{\sum w_i}{\lit{1}{|Z(y)|}\,\hat p(y)}}"
            {' "Z"}
            {' accentColor}}}
        {_during s 17.0 21.0 {_candidates {phase s 17.4 18.0} m mark near}}
        {_during s 22.0 24.0 huge}
        {_during s 23.0 27.0 {pointParts
            {phase s 24.0 25.0}
            {_rule "balance" f"{m_i(y) = \frac{p_i(y)}{\lit{1}{\sum_j p_j(y)}}}"
                {' "sum"}
                {' pColor}}
            {' "sum"}
            accentColor}}
        {_during s 25.0 27.0 {_at _slotC {caption "balanceNote"
            {textKey "biasmath-balance"}
            0.32
            textColor}}}
        {_during s 27.0 31.5 {_rule "talbot" f"{w_i = \frac{\hat p(x_i)}{\lit{1}{\sum_j p_j(x_i)}}}"
            {' "sum"}
            {' pColor}}}
        {_during s 28.0 31.5 {_grid s m}}}}]

The scene

Fn([Float], List(Mob)). The plot as the bias values draw it, its legend, and what the sentence at `biasStage` adds.
$[# {_scene s}
    [# m {round {biasCandidates}}]
    [# near {biasNearZero}]
    [# mark {biasMark}]
    [# reveal {biasReveal}]
    [# c {biasCurves m {biasWeight} near}]
    [# ax {axesIn _plotBox {axisRange 0.0 1.0 0.25} {axisRange 0.0 4.0 1.0}}]
    {flatten {' {_plot ax reveal mark near c} {_legends reveal} {_beside s mark m near ax c}}}]

The hook

Fn([Float], List(Mob)). The 1D example at stage `biasStage`.
$[# biasMath {: {^ {t} {_scene {biasStage}}} Math}]
